1
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:05,463
Your age is 27?

2
00:00:05,547 --> 00:00:06,464
I'm 20.

3
00:00:06,548 --> 00:00:07,674
You have a wife and child?

4
00:00:07,757 --> 00:00:08,883
I live alone.

5
00:00:08,967 --> 00:00:10,051
You like curry?

6
00:00:10,135 --> 00:00:11,344
I like ramen.

7
00:00:11,428 --> 00:00:14,055
CAN PSYCHIC POWERS EXPOSE?

8
00:00:16,099 --> 00:00:18,727
Santa Dodoria sure is something.

9
00:00:18,810 --> 00:00:20,353
So flamboyantly wrong.

10
00:00:20,437 --> 00:00:23,314
There's no way such a young idol
could have a wife and a kid.

11
00:00:23,398 --> 00:00:25,817
Even I can see that.

12
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:28,194
Is it okay to air that as-is?

13
00:00:28,278 --> 00:00:29,863
Should be okay.

14
00:00:29,946 --> 00:00:33,074
Nobody would be so pissed off
at a local program like this one.

15
00:00:33,825 --> 00:00:34,492
VACANT

16
00:00:34,576 --> 00:00:35,201
CARRYING PASSENGERS

17
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:48,423
You're Santa Dodoria, aren't you?

18
00:00:49,007 --> 00:00:50,884
I saw you on TV the other day.

19
00:00:50,967 --> 00:00:54,054
Do you really have psychic powers?

20
00:00:54,554 --> 00:00:56,890
Here's fine. Drop me off.

21
00:00:56,973 --> 00:00:58,266
Huh?

22
00:01:00,810 --> 00:01:05,023
It's not like I'm trying to insult you
or anything. I just wanted you to show me.

23
00:01:05,106 --> 00:01:07,567
If you don't wanna die,
hurry on and scram.

24
00:01:35,804 --> 00:01:40,266
Come on now, I thought you
brought over yet another scumbag.

25
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:42,060
But this one isn't even human.

26
00:01:42,685 --> 00:01:43,645
Sheesh.

27
00:01:43,728 --> 00:01:46,606
My grandkid only brings problems in.

28
00:01:46,689 --> 00:01:49,526
My skin's gonna get dry
from all the stress.

29
00:01:51,444 --> 00:01:53,530
Come on. Bring it on.

30
00:03:33,421 --> 00:03:36,257
That was close! You're super fast!

31
00:03:36,841 --> 00:03:39,719
But things happened just as I predicted.

32
00:03:40,345 --> 00:03:42,972
I thought you'd come around
to my blind spot.

33
00:03:44,015 --> 00:03:47,644
You fell into the trap
that I had set up beforehand.

34
00:03:52,690 --> 00:03:56,486
If you cross that line, you'll die.

35
00:03:56,569 --> 00:03:58,571
That's a barrier right there.

36
00:04:00,406 --> 00:04:02,992
When you drive a warding nail
inside this circle,

37
00:04:03,076 --> 00:04:05,703
the inside of the circle
turns into a barrier.

38
00:04:05,787 --> 00:04:07,497
But if you drive it outside the circle,

39
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:10,166
the area outside of the circle
becomes the barrier.

40
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:16,631
The reason you couldn't touch me
was because I was protected by a barrier.

41
00:04:26,349 --> 00:04:29,352
I'll make sure to eat and kill you.

42
00:04:29,435 --> 00:04:32,981
Don't think
you can keep me trapped forever.

43
00:04:33,064 --> 00:04:37,443
I don't wanna trap you. I wanna kill you.

44
00:04:45,076 --> 00:04:47,829
Come on, stand your ground, will ya?

45
00:04:47,912 --> 00:04:49,706
You're gonna cross that line!

46
00:04:51,833 --> 00:04:53,459
What's wrong?

47
00:04:53,543 --> 00:04:57,130
When you're in there, you can't make use
of your speed that you're so proud of.

48
00:04:57,213 --> 00:04:59,007
You scummy old hag!

49
00:04:59,090 --> 00:05:02,552
Did an old hag just call
another old hag a scummy old hag?

50
00:05:03,177 --> 00:05:04,971
That pisses me off.

51
00:05:08,182 --> 00:05:12,103
If you burn me,
this guy that I cursed will die, too.

52
00:05:15,148 --> 00:05:18,943
I'll kill off all scumbags
who deceive my grandkid.

53
00:05:19,485 --> 00:05:21,112
Even if they're human.

54
00:05:23,948 --> 00:05:24,824
Bye.

55
00:05:24,907 --> 00:05:27,368
Scummy old hag!

56
00:05:39,088 --> 00:05:39,922
Okarun!

57
00:05:41,799 --> 00:05:43,468
Hey, you were home?

58
00:05:43,551 --> 00:05:46,888
Shut up. I'm watching <i>The Idiot Shogun</i>.

59
00:05:47,513 --> 00:05:50,683
Anyway, I have something
to talk about with you.

60
00:05:50,767 --> 00:05:52,769
You went to a spiritual hotspot?

61
00:05:54,270 --> 00:05:55,480
I did.

62
00:05:55,563 --> 00:05:58,149
Not me, but a friend.

63
00:05:58,232 --> 00:05:59,192
Why?

64
00:06:00,151 --> 00:06:01,319
"Why?"

65
00:06:01,402 --> 00:06:04,989
Because we were talking
and that's how things ended up.

66
00:06:08,242 --> 00:06:10,369
<i>The Idiot Shogun</i>
is Japan's national treasure.

67
00:06:10,453 --> 00:06:12,455
Hey, were you listening?

68
00:06:13,039 --> 00:06:14,916
Anyway, did you see a guy?

69
00:06:14,999 --> 00:06:17,418
He'll be in big trouble if I'm not around!

70
00:06:18,795 --> 00:06:20,963
If you're talking about the evil spirit,
I killed it.

71
00:06:22,673 --> 00:06:25,426
An evil spirit? What kind?
Did it have glasses on?

72
00:06:26,052 --> 00:06:31,390
Come on, you don't even believe in ghosts.

73
00:06:32,391 --> 00:06:35,144
Besides, I'm a fake spirit medium.

74
00:06:38,147 --> 00:06:40,525
How long are you gonna hold
that grudge, you scummy old hag.

75
00:06:40,608 --> 00:06:43,986
Something really bad might happen,
so just answer me!

76
00:06:44,070 --> 00:06:47,198
Stop it. Don't believe in those stories.

77
00:06:47,281 --> 00:06:50,743
{\an8}There are no evil spirits, and I'm a fake.

78
00:06:55,915 --> 00:06:57,125
{\an8}Grandma.

79
00:07:02,088 --> 00:07:05,049
{\an8}I'm sorry. I was wrong.

80
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:09,220
{\an8}So please tell me.
What did you do to the evil spirit?

81
00:07:10,513 --> 00:07:12,140
Head over to the main shrine.

82
00:07:12,807 --> 00:07:14,225
Scummy old hag!

83
00:07:14,892 --> 00:07:17,770
If something's wrong with Okarun,
I'll never forgive you!

84
00:07:19,939 --> 00:07:22,066
<i>I didn't want to miss my chance.</i>

85
00:07:22,150 --> 00:07:26,779
<i>He was just an occult freak</i>
<i>who simply wanted friends.</i>

86
00:07:26,863 --> 00:07:28,114
<i>It's my fault.</i>

87
00:07:28,197 --> 00:07:30,700
<i>Because I forced him to go to that place!</i>

88
00:07:31,242 --> 00:07:32,326
<i>I'm sorry, Okarun!</i>

89
00:07:33,661 --> 00:07:34,537
Okarun!

90
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:41,002
Miss Ayase! I'm so glad!

91
00:07:41,085 --> 00:07:44,088
I thought that I'd murdered you
or something.

92
00:07:45,047 --> 00:07:46,132
Huh?

93
00:07:46,215 --> 00:07:47,717
Wait. Miss Ayase?

94
00:07:48,759 --> 00:07:50,178
Miss Ayase?

95
00:07:51,095 --> 00:07:53,097
You're still alive and well,
scumbag four-eyes!

96
00:07:53,181 --> 00:07:54,765
What? What's up with that?

97
00:07:54,849 --> 00:07:57,143
Well, I'm sorry I'm still alive!

98
00:07:59,353 --> 00:08:01,397
I'm so irritated.

99
00:08:07,028 --> 00:08:10,490
Since when have you
started being friends with monsters?

100
00:08:10,573 --> 00:08:11,574
You scared me!

101
00:08:12,158 --> 00:08:14,702
The curse won't kick in
as long as he's in there.

102
00:08:14,785 --> 00:08:18,331
But one step outside,
and he's back to a monster.

103
00:08:18,414 --> 00:08:21,918
What was that about killing him off?
You lied to me.

104
00:08:22,001 --> 00:08:26,214
You seemed pretty desperate.
You into brats like that?

105
00:08:26,297 --> 00:08:27,465
No way!

106
00:08:28,049 --> 00:08:31,427
Turbo Granny took his you-know-what.

107
00:08:31,511 --> 00:08:36,098
And she told me that as long as
she has it, his curse won't be lifted.

108
00:08:36,682 --> 00:08:41,437
I'm responsible for what happened to him,
so I just want to do something about it.

109
00:08:41,521 --> 00:08:43,564
Oh, I see. So you do like him.

110
00:08:43,648 --> 00:08:45,107
I didn't say that!

111
00:08:45,691 --> 00:08:49,320
Anyway, I can use psychic powers now.

112
00:08:49,403 --> 00:08:51,239
What the hell are you talkin' about?

113
00:08:51,322 --> 00:08:53,533
I went to this place where UFOs show up.

114
00:08:53,616 --> 00:08:56,118
A lot of stuff happened there,
and now I can use powers.

115
00:08:56,202 --> 00:08:58,246
But UFOs don't exist.

116
00:08:58,329 --> 00:09:02,792
I totally get that reaction.
I was just like that until yesterday.

117
00:09:02,875 --> 00:09:05,920
Anyway, it's true
that I can use psychic powers now.

118
00:09:06,003 --> 00:09:09,006
And if I'm not holding back
Okarun's curse with it, he goes wild.

119
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:11,259
I'm sure psychic powers exist.

120
00:09:11,342 --> 00:09:14,220
I don't know what your criteria
for believing stuff is.

121
00:09:14,804 --> 00:09:17,765
Anyway, Turbo Granny, huh?

122
00:09:18,307 --> 00:09:20,810
You sure got your hands
on a troublesome one.

123
00:09:21,394 --> 00:09:24,355
<i>In the past, she used to be called</i>
<i>the Hundred Kilo Granny.</i>

124
00:09:24,438 --> 00:09:27,817
<i>She's a modern </i>yokai <i>monster that</i>
<i>wreaked havoc all over the country.</i>

125
00:09:28,568 --> 00:09:30,987
<i>And I heard such an elusive entity</i>

126
00:09:31,070 --> 00:09:34,365
<i>had been dwelling</i>
<i>for some time in that tunnel.</i>

127
00:09:34,448 --> 00:09:36,826
<i>I went over there once</i>
<i>to check things out.</i>

128
00:09:36,909 --> 00:09:37,827
KEEP OUT

129
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:40,162
<i>It was most strange.</i>

130
00:09:40,913 --> 00:09:42,707
{\an8}<i>I couldn't even get near the tunnel</i>

131
00:09:42,790 --> 00:09:45,501
{\an8}<i>because of just how strong</i>
<i>the spiritual power was.</i>

132
00:09:46,460 --> 00:09:48,838
<i>You know about location-bound spirits?</i>

133
00:09:49,672 --> 00:09:51,299
<i>They're spirits that stay</i>

134
00:09:51,382 --> 00:09:54,051
<i>in particular locations</i>
<i>that they have strong attachments to.</i>

135
00:09:54,635 --> 00:09:57,930
<i>They're basically the strongest</i>
<i>within their territories.</i>

136
00:09:58,806 --> 00:10:02,643
<i>No spirit medium would go up</i>
<i>against a location-bound spirit.</i>

137
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:07,940
<i>There was a location-bound spirit</i>
<i>inside that tunnel.</i>

138
00:10:09,609 --> 00:10:11,986
<i>Do you know what that means?</i>

139
00:10:14,989 --> 00:10:18,951
<i>Turbo Granny and that</i>
<i>location-bound spirit had fused together.</i>

140
00:10:24,832 --> 00:10:26,876
Don't try to fight against it.

141
00:10:26,959 --> 00:10:29,837
I don't want to lose my dear grandchild.

142
00:10:33,299 --> 00:10:35,968
You're not directly involved with it,
either.

143
00:10:36,052 --> 00:10:37,970
So forget about him.

144
00:10:40,014 --> 00:10:41,974
You should return to everyday life.

145
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:49,398
I wonder what the Mr. Ken I love
would do in times like this.

146
00:10:49,482 --> 00:10:52,443
When I can't decide, that's what I think.

147
00:10:53,027 --> 00:10:55,613
I've never had regrets
by choosing this way.

148
00:10:55,696 --> 00:11:00,076
And if this was Mr. Ken,
I'm 100% positive he'd go in and help.

149
00:11:00,159 --> 00:11:02,036
So that's what I'm gonna do!

150
00:11:03,913 --> 00:11:05,998
Mr. Ken, you say?

151
00:11:06,082 --> 00:11:08,793
-You're totally in love with that kid!
-No, that's not what I mean!

152
00:11:08,876 --> 00:11:10,211
I wasn't talking about him!

153
00:11:10,294 --> 00:11:13,047
Hey, she's confessing your love to you.
How do you feel?

154
00:11:13,130 --> 00:11:16,467
I told you that's not what I mean!
I'm talking about the actor!

155
00:11:16,550 --> 00:11:19,512
Looks like I got no choice
if you're gonna go that far.

156
00:11:20,971 --> 00:11:23,391
Go play tag with Turbo Granny.

157
00:11:23,933 --> 00:11:27,061
That thing has absolute confidence
in its running.

158
00:11:27,144 --> 00:11:30,564
A few random taunts
and it's sure to take the challenge.

159
00:11:30,648 --> 00:11:32,358
Now this is where the problem starts.

160
00:11:32,441 --> 00:11:35,027
The location-bound spirit's territory
is all of Shono City.

161
00:11:35,111 --> 00:11:39,448
You have to lure Turbo Granny outside
of the city without getting caught.

162
00:11:39,532 --> 00:11:41,409
If you can drag it away
from its territory,

163
00:11:41,492 --> 00:11:45,579
it will get weak and even you guys
will be able to defeat it.

164
00:11:45,663 --> 00:11:48,374
Oh no, look at these feeble legs.

165
00:11:48,457 --> 00:11:51,377
There's no way in hell
I can play tag against Turbo Granny.

166
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:52,878
Instead of doing something like that,

167
00:11:52,962 --> 00:11:55,214
can't you make something
like those barriers and deal with it?

168
00:11:55,297 --> 00:11:57,341
Like putting one up at the tunnel.

169
00:11:59,510 --> 00:12:01,137
I can't do that.

170
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:02,972
I can't help out to begin with.

171
00:12:03,055 --> 00:12:04,181
Huh? What's up with that?

172
00:12:04,765 --> 00:12:09,562
<i>My barrier spells only borrow the powers</i>
<i>of the gods that live on this land.</i>

173
00:12:09,645 --> 00:12:13,649
<i>Once we leave Kamigoe City where we live,</i>
<i>I can't use these powers.</i>

174
00:12:13,732 --> 00:12:16,485
Oh, so we have our own territory, too.

175
00:12:16,569 --> 00:12:19,363
All lands have their own gods.

176
00:12:19,447 --> 00:12:22,491
The problem is whether you're playing
a home or an away game.

177
00:12:22,575 --> 00:12:25,744
In any case, this is the only way
to defeat Turbo Granny.

178
00:12:25,828 --> 00:12:27,329
If you start physically training now,

179
00:12:27,413 --> 00:12:29,623
you should be able to become
fast enough to run away from her.

180
00:12:29,707 --> 00:12:31,375
Are you seriously saying that?

181
00:12:31,459 --> 00:12:33,169
No matter how hard I tried,

182
00:12:33,252 --> 00:12:35,671
I couldn't even make it
to the prefecture finals for track meets!

183
00:12:35,754 --> 00:12:37,006
I'm not talking about you.

184
00:12:37,089 --> 00:12:37,923
Huh?

185
00:12:38,424 --> 00:12:40,593
-I'm talking about him.
-Oh, I see!

186
00:12:41,510 --> 00:12:44,054
You're finally including me
into the conversation?

187
00:12:44,138 --> 00:12:45,806
Sorry, I forgot.

188
00:12:45,890 --> 00:12:48,309
But Okarun, you have no stamina.

189
00:12:48,392 --> 00:12:49,768
None at all.

190
00:12:49,852 --> 00:12:52,688
And I have to keep control
over your curse.

191
00:12:52,771 --> 00:12:54,773
Then he needs to run piggy-backing Momo.

192
00:12:54,857 --> 00:12:56,817
Miss Ayase, how much do you weigh?

193
00:12:56,901 --> 00:12:58,611
Hey, do ya wanna die?

194
00:12:58,694 --> 00:13:00,279
Oh no, it's just impossible!

195
00:13:00,362 --> 00:13:03,824
My limit for going full strength
in cursed mode is about twice!

196
00:13:03,908 --> 00:13:04,950
Right!

197
00:13:05,034 --> 00:13:07,453
Then train so that you can
always be at full strength.

198
00:13:07,536 --> 00:13:08,787
Get to it. Push-ups, sit-ups,

199
00:13:08,871 --> 00:13:11,248
back extensions, and squats.
Five sets, 100 reps each.

200
00:13:11,332 --> 00:13:12,750
-Huh?
-Do it.

201
00:13:12,833 --> 00:13:15,544
And Momo, same goes
for your psychic powers.

202
00:13:15,628 --> 00:13:18,339
You need to power them up
more than what they are now.

203
00:13:20,841 --> 00:13:25,513
As I can't be of any help,
you guys simply have to get stronger.

204
00:13:25,596 --> 00:13:28,057
So I will be training the two of you.

205
00:13:28,849 --> 00:13:31,560
Go to sleep for today.
We'll start tomorrow.

206
00:13:31,644 --> 00:13:33,687
Four-eyes, start your physical training
right now.

207
00:13:33,771 --> 00:13:35,606
Oh, okay.

208
00:13:36,482 --> 00:13:38,442
Your granny is so young.

209
00:13:38,984 --> 00:13:40,444
Isn't she annoying?

210
00:13:44,698 --> 00:13:46,951
Miss Ayase, I'm so sorry.

211
00:13:48,911 --> 00:13:51,080
When I fought that big thing,

212
00:13:51,163 --> 00:13:55,292
I was honestly too desperate
to think of anyone other than myself.

213
00:13:55,376 --> 00:13:56,835
I'm really sorry.

214
00:13:56,919 --> 00:13:59,296
Oh, there's nothing
you could've done about that.

215
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:02,258
But Miss Ayase, you were different.

216
00:14:02,341 --> 00:14:05,469
You saved me and defeated the monster.

217
00:14:06,053 --> 00:14:12,268
But if something like that happens again,
I'll do my best so that I can save you.

218
00:14:12,893 --> 00:14:16,188
So please don't be disappointed with me.

219
00:14:16,272 --> 00:14:19,483
Please, don't stop being a friend.

220
00:14:20,985 --> 00:14:23,696
I wouldn't be disappointed.
You're overthinking.

221
00:14:26,365 --> 00:14:29,660
Then why did you slam the door earlier?

222
00:14:29,743 --> 00:14:30,828
W-Well, that was…

223
00:14:30,911 --> 00:14:33,873
See, there you go!
You really were disappointed!

224
00:14:33,956 --> 00:14:35,457
I said I wasn't!

225
00:14:35,541 --> 00:14:38,794
But like, I am right now!
You're such a pain!

226
00:14:38,878 --> 00:14:40,379
I'm sorry.

227
00:14:40,462 --> 00:14:43,215
You were pretty awesome
when you were fighting.

228
00:14:44,341 --> 00:14:46,468
But you're kinda dense, Okarun.

229
00:14:46,552 --> 00:14:48,804
I'll probably be saving you
next time, too!

230
00:14:51,265 --> 00:14:52,808
You sleep there for today.

231
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:54,518
I'll bring you a futon right now.

232
00:14:59,940 --> 00:15:00,983
Miss Ayase!

233
00:15:02,735 --> 00:15:04,612
Um, well…

234
00:15:07,072 --> 00:15:08,407
I'm…

235
00:15:10,534 --> 00:15:13,454
really thirsty, so can I have some water?

236
00:15:15,289 --> 00:15:18,167
Can I take this barley tea?

237
00:15:18,250 --> 00:15:19,209
Sure thing.

238
00:15:20,002 --> 00:15:22,212
<i>We have some shocking news</i>
<i>that just came in!</i>

239
00:15:22,296 --> 00:15:23,756
{\an8}<i>It came out into the open</i>

240
00:15:23,839 --> 00:15:25,883
{\an8}<i>that popular idol Shoma</i>
<i>had a secret child!</i>

241
00:15:25,966 --> 00:15:30,012
{\an8}<i>And his age wasn't 20, but actually 27!</i>

242
00:15:30,679 --> 00:15:35,643
{\an8}They need to correct his favorite food
from ramen to curry, too!

243
00:15:35,726 --> 00:15:36,644
{\an8}<i>Furthermore…</i>

244
00:15:36,727 --> 00:15:37,853
{\an8}<i>…he and his partner…</i>

245
00:15:37,937 --> 00:15:38,604
{\an8}<i>…have not…</i>

246
00:15:38,687 --> 00:15:39,480
{\an8}<i>…formally submitted…</i>

247
00:15:39,563 --> 00:15:40,481
{\an8}<i>…a marriage license.</i>

248
00:15:45,444 --> 00:15:48,030
I could care less about that news.

249
00:15:49,490 --> 00:15:50,699
Miss Ayase!

250
00:15:50,783 --> 00:15:54,620
Crap! Okarun wants to go to the bathroom!

251
00:15:54,703 --> 00:15:55,955
Just go.

252
00:15:56,038 --> 00:15:58,540
No, but this is seriously bad news!

253
00:15:58,624 --> 00:15:59,875
If something blocks my view

254
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:01,794
and I can't see Okarun,
my spell on him breaks!

255
00:16:01,877 --> 00:16:05,381
In other words, I have to watch Okarun
as he relieves himself!

256
00:16:05,464 --> 00:16:06,423
Then watch him.

257
00:16:06,507 --> 00:16:08,509
I'd never want to watch!

258
00:16:08,592 --> 00:16:09,969
Who would show you, anyway?

259
00:16:10,052 --> 00:16:12,805
That tramples upon someone else's dignity!

260
00:16:12,888 --> 00:16:14,848
Hey! Don't look away!

261
00:16:17,393 --> 00:16:19,103
Don't you have any good ideas?

262
00:16:19,186 --> 00:16:20,062
Dunno.

263
00:16:20,854 --> 00:16:23,983
How the hell are you holding
the curse back to begin with, anyway?

264
00:16:24,066 --> 00:16:25,275
Let's see…

265
00:16:25,359 --> 00:16:26,777
How do I put it…

266
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:29,738
It's like I can see an aura around Okarun.

267
00:16:29,822 --> 00:16:30,656
An aura?

268
00:16:30,739 --> 00:16:35,494
And when I crush that aura
with my hands, the aura shrinks.

269
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:38,247
And the curse subsides, I guess?

270
00:16:38,956 --> 00:16:42,292
Everyone has some kind of aura,
and they come in all sorts of colors.

271
00:16:42,376 --> 00:16:44,753
I see them on the trees
and rocks there too.

272
00:16:44,837 --> 00:16:50,134
I can grab all those auras and move them
at my will, though only in a small area.

273
00:16:50,217 --> 00:16:54,471
I see. I thought psychic powers
were a lot more omnipotent.

274
00:16:54,555 --> 00:16:56,348
Sounds like they're quite limited.

275
00:16:58,100 --> 00:17:02,312
It was a lot more amazing the moment
the powers awoke inside of me.

276
00:17:02,396 --> 00:17:05,315
<i>That was when everything I imagined</i>
<i>turned into reality,</i>

277
00:17:05,399 --> 00:17:07,735
<i>like I was invincible!</i>

278
00:17:07,818 --> 00:17:12,406
But that went away real quick.
I can only grab auras and stuff now.

279
00:17:12,489 --> 00:17:14,116
Momo, close your eyes for a bit.

280
00:17:14,199 --> 00:17:17,369
No way. If I do that,
my spell will be lifted.

281
00:17:17,453 --> 00:17:20,581
Basically, the problem
is the reliance on your vision.

282
00:17:20,664 --> 00:17:24,585
Try using all of your senses,
such as touch.

283
00:17:24,668 --> 00:17:28,047
The fact that you can grab the aura
means that it's tactile.

284
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:31,759
So close those eyes
and try feeling the aura with your skin.

285
00:17:34,428 --> 00:17:36,305
Slowly, feel it around you.

286
00:17:41,310 --> 00:17:42,603
So cold.

287
00:17:43,312 --> 00:17:44,146
How am I doing?

288
00:17:44,855 --> 00:17:45,647
Yeah.

289
00:17:46,231 --> 00:17:47,107
He's transformed.

290
00:17:47,191 --> 00:17:48,358
No good.

291
00:17:48,442 --> 00:17:49,610
Well, crap.

292
00:17:49,693 --> 00:17:53,906
That really pushed me close to the limit!
I won't last much longer!

293
00:17:53,989 --> 00:17:56,075
What are you gonna do, Momo?
He's gonna poop any moment.

294
00:17:56,158 --> 00:17:57,785
You're the one who told me to try that!

295
00:17:57,868 --> 00:18:00,162
I don't want to be watched
as I relieve myself!

296
00:18:00,245 --> 00:18:03,582
But I wanna pee in my pants even less!

297
00:18:03,665 --> 00:18:04,666
Hold on!

298
00:18:04,750 --> 00:18:05,959
I'm gonna borrow your bathro--

299
00:18:07,503 --> 00:18:11,548
You've got some nerve to take a dump
in someone else's house, punk!

300
00:18:11,632 --> 00:18:12,841
I'm pretty desperate too, you know!

301
00:18:13,425 --> 00:18:15,344
Why you little…
Who said they'd lend you the bathroom?

302
00:18:15,427 --> 00:18:18,680
Are you an absolute idiot?
I can piss right here if you want!

303
00:18:18,764 --> 00:18:19,765
Let me in on this too!

304
00:18:19,848 --> 00:18:21,975
Don't think you can run faster
than me in this house!

305
00:18:22,059 --> 00:18:23,644
Outta my way! Or you'll have a disaster!

306
00:18:24,770 --> 00:18:26,522
Not bad, Ken Takakura!

307
00:18:26,605 --> 00:18:27,940
This one is mine!

308
00:18:28,023 --> 00:18:29,358
Not letting you!

309
00:18:32,569 --> 00:18:33,862
This is humiliating.

310
00:18:33,946 --> 00:18:35,572
Says you.

311
00:18:35,656 --> 00:18:38,826
I had looked forward to experiences
unknown until now,

312
00:18:38,909 --> 00:18:41,120
like getting abducted by aliens.

313
00:18:41,203 --> 00:18:42,037
Seriously?

314
00:18:42,121 --> 00:18:43,997
But this is just too much.

315
00:18:44,081 --> 00:18:47,000
I want to hurry up
and be released from this curse.

316
00:18:47,584 --> 00:18:52,214
Momo, you said that you were invincible
when your powers first awoke.

317
00:18:52,297 --> 00:18:53,132
Yeah.

318
00:18:53,215 --> 00:18:56,176
That's likely your original power.

319
00:18:56,260 --> 00:18:59,596
And it seems for some reason,
that power has been sealed off.

320
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:01,557
What's with that? It sounds kinda cool.

321
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:03,475
It's a pain in the butt.

322
00:19:03,559 --> 00:19:06,854
You have to unleash it
bit by bit through training,

323
00:19:06,937 --> 00:19:09,606
and we don't know how long that will take.

324
00:19:09,690 --> 00:19:10,732
Though it's okay

325
00:19:10,816 --> 00:19:13,735
because it looks like that boy's
physical makeover will take some time.

326
00:19:13,819 --> 00:19:16,280
I have to be watched while going
to the bathroom for a while?

327
00:19:16,363 --> 00:19:17,823
That's my line…

328
00:19:20,450 --> 00:19:22,661
Grandma, it's here! Turbo Granny!

329
00:19:22,744 --> 00:19:23,704
Grandma?

330
00:19:23,787 --> 00:19:25,038
Grandma?

331
00:19:25,622 --> 00:19:28,417
Damn you! What the hell
are you doing to Grandma?

332
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:34,298
I'm letting her choose her cause of death.
A heart attack or a stroke.

333
00:19:34,381 --> 00:19:38,760
My curse is contagious through this brat.

334
00:19:39,344 --> 00:19:42,806
{\an8}Any human this brat sees,
I can curse to death.

335
00:19:43,473 --> 00:19:48,854
Don't underestimate me.
I'm not gonna give you any time.

336
00:19:48,937 --> 00:19:50,939
Come to the tunnel tonight.

337
00:19:51,023 --> 00:19:56,403
Otherwise, I'll use this brat to curse
everyone around there to death.

338
00:19:56,486 --> 00:19:58,363
That's tonight.

339
00:19:58,447 --> 00:20:00,324
Got that?

340
00:20:03,202 --> 00:20:04,036
A nosebleed…

341
00:20:04,620 --> 00:20:05,537
Grandma!

342
00:20:05,621 --> 00:20:07,039
What's this?

343
00:20:07,122 --> 00:20:08,707
You're bleeding from your ears, too!

344
00:20:08,790 --> 00:20:10,626
Does your head hurt or something?

345
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:14,838
Momo. Let's hear about what just happened.

346
00:20:17,049 --> 00:20:18,508
<i>Am I seriously wearing this?</i>

347
00:20:18,592 --> 00:20:20,385
<i>It's hard to see in front of me.</i>

348
00:20:20,469 --> 00:20:22,846
<i>That's a bulletproof vest</i>
<i>against evil spirits.</i>

349
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:24,306
<i>Make sure to keep them on.</i>

350
00:20:24,389 --> 00:20:26,266
<i>If you let your guard down,</i>
<i>you'll die quite easily.</i>

351
00:20:26,350 --> 00:20:30,229
<i>I know that! Despite how we look,</i>
<i>we did defeat aliens!</i>

352
00:20:30,312 --> 00:20:34,191
{\an8}There's no such thing as aliens.
Quit horsing around.

353
00:20:34,274 --> 00:20:35,609
{\an8}Oh, okay.

354
00:20:36,193 --> 00:20:40,614
{\an8}You bring all the trouble home in
the first place because you're like that.

355
00:20:41,156 --> 00:20:43,242
{\an8}You've never listened to me
ever since you were a little kid.

356
00:20:43,325 --> 00:20:47,621
{\an8}Man, so annoying!
Grandma's nagging is annoying.

357
00:20:47,704 --> 00:20:48,705
{\an8}Let's go, Okarun.

358
00:20:52,626 --> 00:20:53,627
Momo!

359
00:20:53,710 --> 00:20:55,796
What now? You're so naggy.

360
00:21:01,301 --> 00:21:02,678
Don't die.

361
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:05,514
Yeah.

362
00:21:11,061 --> 00:21:12,688
<i>I beg of you.</i>

363
00:21:13,438 --> 00:21:16,608
<i>Please, protect those two.</i>

364
00:21:18,485 --> 00:21:20,028
Why are we going by train?

365
00:21:20,112 --> 00:21:21,738
It's too far by bicycle!

366
00:21:21,822 --> 00:21:24,199
And you don't want to use up your stamina
before we get there!

367
00:21:24,783 --> 00:21:27,077
You seriously aren't getting off
the hook, Turbo Granny!

368
00:21:27,828 --> 00:21:29,997
-I'm sorry, this is all for…
-No way!

369
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:36,253
<i>That hag tried to hurt</i>
<i>something dear to me!</i>

370
00:21:36,336 --> 00:21:39,923
I'm gonna beat Turbo Granny into a pulp!

371
00:23:12,224 --> 00:23:15,102
Hold on, Miss Ayase!
You shouldn't do that here!

372
00:23:15,185 --> 00:23:16,937
I want to hurry up and take these off.

373
00:23:17,020 --> 00:23:18,688
Is it okay to do that?

374
00:23:18,772 --> 00:23:21,858
It's a battle uniform to protect yourself
from evil spirits, right?

375
00:23:21,942 --> 00:23:23,360
Your grandmother said keep it on.

376
00:23:23,443 --> 00:23:25,195
Who the hell would wear
something like that?

377
00:23:27,531 --> 00:23:29,950
Fashion is the battle uniform for <i>gyarus!</i>

378
00:23:30,033 --> 00:23:32,536
I can't get hyped up unless I wear
the clothes I want to wear!

379
00:23:35,413 --> 00:23:36,998
Why are you smiling?

380
00:23:37,082 --> 00:23:38,834
Isn't this kinda fun?

381
00:23:38,917 --> 00:23:42,045
Not at all. I feel like I'm about to puke.

382
00:23:43,505 --> 00:23:45,215
<i>Who's a gaudy hag, ya scummy old hag!</i>

383
00:23:45,298 --> 00:23:46,299
<i>What's got into you?</i>

384
00:23:46,383 --> 00:23:48,760
<i>Turbo Granny called me</i>
<i>a gaudy hag the other day!</i>

385
00:23:48,844 --> 00:23:49,803
<i>Huh? That really happened?</i>

386
00:23:49,886 --> 00:23:51,596
<i>You were kinda crazy</i>
<i>from that curse, Okarun!</i>

387
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:53,014
<i>All right, let's go!</i>

388
00:23:53,098 --> 00:23:55,308
<i>Next episode,</i>
<i>"Kicking Turbo Granny's Ass."</i>

389
00:23:55,392 --> 00:23:57,936
<i>But in the end,</i>
<i>it's a bit embarrassing to go by train.</i>
